  "has_animal_human_comparison": false,
  "evidence": "The study systematically reviewed preclinical animal models of sepsis to evaluate the efficacy of mesenchymal stem cell (MSC) therapy prior to initiating a first-in-human trial. All measurements provided are within-animal comparisons, evaluating the efficacy of MSC therapy in animal models of sepsis compared to control treatments within those same models, or assessing characteristics of the animal studies themselves. There are no direct comparisons made between animal results and human outcomes.",
  "comparison_type": "within-animal-only",
  "reason": "The study focuses exclusively on analyzing data from preclinical animal models of sepsis. All reported measurements, such as odds ratios for mortality and failure rates of replication, are comparisons made within these animal models or relate to the generalizability and reporting quality of preclinical studies. There is no mention or reporting of any direct comparison between the outcomes observed in animal models and any human clinical trial results or human patient data."
